<article class="env-lemma" id="0DDE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DDE">Lemma <span data-tag="0DDE">59.91.12</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a proper morphism of schemes. Let $g : Y' \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Set $X' = Y' \times _ Y X$ and denote $f' : X' \to Y'$ and $g' : X' \to X$ the projections. Let $E \in D^+(X_{\acute{e}tale})$ have torsion cohomology sheaves. Then the base change map (<a href="/tag/0A2A" data-tag="0A2A">59.91.5.2</a>) $g^{-1}Rf_*E \to Rf'_*(g')^{-1}E$ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a simple consequence of the proper base change theorem (Theorem <a href="/tag/095T" data-tag="095T">59.91.11</a>) using the spectral sequences 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{p, q} = R^ pf_*H^ q(E) \quad \text{and}\quad {E'}_2^{p, q} = R^ pf'_*(g')^{-1}H^ q(E)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       converging to $R^ nf_*E$ and $R^ nf'_*(g')^{-1}E$. The spectral sequences are constructed in Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015J" data-tag="015J">13.21.3</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>